(footprint "SW_Kailh_Choc_V1_HotSwap_THT_1.00u_Diode" (version 20221018) (generator pcbnew)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Kailh Choc V1 (PG1350) low profile mechanical keyboard switch, hot-swap socket and through-hole soldering, single-sided mounting. Plate cut lines: User.1=15.60mm square (cosmetic cover, all switches), User.4=13.80mm square with R1.00 corner relief (Kailh Choc V1). Keycap: 1.00u (courtyard 19.00x19.00mm). Series diode pads on back side: pad 3 = anode, pad 4 = cathode (cathode bar on B.SilkS, body outline on B.Fab, cathode points up). Combined hand-soldering land for SOD-123 / SOD-323 / MiniMELF (LL-34, LL4148): 2.0x1.4mm pads at +/-1.6mm axial offset. With the bundled SW_Key_Diode symbol pins 2 and 3 are stacked (one net), so the switch-diode series circuit is complete at schematic level; on the PCB route the short pad 2 - pad 3 track shown by the ratsnest, and wire the matrix to pads 1 and 4.")
  (tags "switch, low_profile, hot_swap, diode")
